/*
 * The three byte-oriented CRCs are computed with lookup tables.
 *
 * A CRC register is updated by one shift-and-conditional-XOR step per message bit. Those steps
 * are linear over GF(2), so the effect of the eight steps for one byte depends only on the
 * eight register bits that the byte is XORed into. Entry i of a table is the result of the
 * eight steps on the value i, which turns the inner loop into one lookup per byte.
 *
 * The tables are written out instead of being computed at start-up: they are constant data
 * that the linker places in flash, the module keeps no state and needs no init call, and a
 * reviewer can compare them with a published table. They cost 256 + 256 + 1024 bytes.
 * tests/unit/test_crc.c recomputes every entry bit by bit from the polynomial.
 *
 * In all functions `data` is only read when `len` is not 0, so a NULL pointer with a length
 * of 0 is a valid empty buffer.
 */

